[32m+[m[32m## Feature Status[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Implemented[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- JavaScript/JSX and React DOM/SVG spatial workspace with pan, zoom, research cards, and editable node connections.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Manual groups/clusters, local browser persistence, and JSON-based `.psychis` import/export.[m
[32m+[m[32m- External search/model integrations and local template fallbacks.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Collision-aware placement and arrangement heuristics; these do not guarantee an optimal or overlap-free layout.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Experimental[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Model-generated graph relationships and follow-up branches.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Model-assisted cluster suggestions and automatic grouping, with proximity-based fallback behavior.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Generated explanations and suggested relationships require source checking; no validated coherence/confidence metric is displayed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Planned / Future Direction[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Local semantic/vector indexing and semantic retrieval over saved research.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Deeper entity/relation extraction with evaluation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- More advanced graph-layout algorithms.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPSYCHIS currently implements a node-and-edge research workspace, not a formal[m
[32m+[m[32mgraph reasoning engine. External services provide model inference and web results;[m
[32m+[m[32mPSYCHIS code manages the workspace interaction, routing, card preparation, links,[m
[32m+[m[32mplacement, and persistence. Example/template cards are illustrative content.[m
